data: {"type":"content_block_delta","index":0,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"**Redis** is fast, and a TTL expires abandoned carts automatically, but it's an extra service to run unless you already have it, and its in-memory data needs persistence configured or carts are lost on restart. **Postgres** keeps carts durable and transactional, lets you query them for abandoned-cart reports and support lookups, and is probably already in your stack, but it adds write load to the main database and needs a cleanup job for old carts. Either way, the cookie should hold only a cart ID.\n\nI recommend **Postgres**, unless you already run Redis with persistence. The one-fewer-service benefit outweighs the speed difference at typical cart volumes.\n\nThe choice is yours. I've filed it as ask **A1** with \"Use Postgres\" (recommended) and \"Use Redis\" buttons. I didn't read or write any files."}}

